  "text": {
    "intro": "Mrs Pell's secondhand bookshop shelves by a system she alone understands, and she has gone to Margate for a fortnight.\nFive volumes are involved. Determine each volume's shelf, keepsake and price.\n- **Volume**: a water-stained atlas, a book of sea shanties, an album of pressed ferns, a beekeeping manual and a guide to fungi.\n- **Shelf** (listed from lower to higher): the bottom shelf, the second shelf, the third shelf, the fourth shelf and the fifth shelf.\n- **Found inside**: a lock of hair, a laundry list, a postcard from Hull, a recipe for quince jelly and a pressed violet.\n- **Pencilled price**: half a crown; seven and six; two shillings; a guinea; and one and six.\nEvery volume has a different shelf, keepsake and price, so within each category every item is used exactly once.",
    "clues": [
      "The volume that contains a pressed violet is higher than the second shelf in shelf order. An album of pressed ferns and the second shelf are exactly three shelves apart in shelf order.",
      "The volume that contains a recipe for quince jelly is not priced at half a crown. The volume that contains a recipe for quince jelly does not sit on the second shelf.",
      "The volume that is priced at seven and six and the second shelf are exactly one shelf apart in shelf order, in one direction or the other.",
      "The second shelf falls somewhere between the volume that contains a postcard from Hull and the volume that is priced at one and six in shelf order.",
      "The volume that contains a postcard from Hull is not priced at half a crown. A water-stained atlas does not contain a postcard from Hull.",
      "The volume that is priced at one and six is exactly one shelf lower than a guide to fungi, with no shelf in between.",
      "The volume that is priced at half a crown is lower than an album of pressed ferns in shelf order.",
      "The volume that is priced at a guinea falls somewhere between the volume that contains a lock of hair and the volume that contains a postcard from Hull in shelf order.",
      "A beekeeping manual and the volume that is priced at one and six both sit at odd-numbered shelves or both at even-numbered shelves.",
      "The volume that is priced at a guinea is exactly one shelf lower than a water-stained atlas, with no shelf in between. A book of sea shanties is not priced at a guinea."
    ]
